    {
      "id": "N-009",
      "when": {
        "before": "^\\s*(?!(?:scadenz[ae]|termin[ei]|udienz[ae]|rat[ae]|pagament[oi]|versament[oi]|saldo|entro|data|rinvio|comparizione|prossim[ao]|nuov[ao])\\b)(?-i:[A-ZÀ-Ý][A-Za-zÀ-ÿ'’.]*(?:\\s+(?:(?:di|del|della|dei|degli|de|in|nel|nell['’]|sul|sull['’]|al|a|d['’]|la|lo|le)\\s*)*[A-ZÀ-Ý][A-Za-zÀ-ÿ'’.]*){0,4}),\\s*(?:(?:l[iì]|addì)\\s+)?$",
        "after_not": "^\\s*,?\\s*(?:ore|alle|h\\.?)\\s*\\d",
        "max_days_after_reference": 7
      },
      "then": {
        "nature": "historical"
      },
      "rationale": "the 'Place, date' line that closes or opens a letter ('Esempio, 05/10/2026') is the date of the document, never a term - also when the transport timestamp is earlier (tampered, or a letter dated the day after). The line must be made of the place alone: one to five capitalised words, lower-case particles allowed between them; a term noun is not a place. A document is dated around the day it is sent: a 'Place, date' more than 7 days after the transport date, or followed by a time of day, is not treated as a dateline (it may be a hearing written as 'Tribunale di X, date ore ...'): unknown, surfaced",
