    {
      "id": "N-V01",
      "applies_to_nature": "actionable",
      "when": {
        "after": "\\b(?:non|né|mai)\\b|(?<![\\w’'])(?:è|e['’]|sono|era|erano|sarà|saranno|viene|vengono|verrà|verranno|resta|restano|rimane|rimangono|risulta|risultano|intende|intendono|intendersi)(?![\\w’'])(?!\\s+(?:stat[oaie]\\s+)?(?:fissat|confermat|stabilit|previst|calendarizzat)[oaie]\\b)"
      },
      "then": {
        "nature": "RECUPERARE"
      },
      "rationale": "a cue before the date says 'this is a term'; if the same sentence goes on, after the date, with a negation or with a predicate (è / viene / resta / risulta / si intende + ...), the sentence says something about that term that the cue rule did not read - it may cancel it (è annullata, è revocata), move it (è rinviata al ..., viene anticipata) or deny it (non si terrà). The date is then of unknown nature: surfaced, never driving, and the deadline is RECUPERARE. A predicate that only confirms the term (è fissata, resta confermata, è stata stabilita) does not veto. Applies to every actionable reading, v2.0 cue rules included. N-004 (explicit 'è scaduto', 'è stato revocato' -> historical) is decided before any actionable rule and is not affected",
